### ==============================================================================
### SAP SuccessFactors Employee Central OData v2 Batch Ingestion Suite
### Module: 04-CPI-Integrations-and-OData
### Author: VPR11 | Vaibhav Paithankar
### Description: Atomic Multipart $batch Execution (PerPerson, EmpEmployment, EmpJob)
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = https://apisalesdemo4.successfactors.com/odata/v2
@apiUser = SF_CPI_INTEGRATION@CompanyProd
@apiPassword = {{SF_API_PASSWORD}}
@boundary = batch_sf_migration_boundary_001
@changesetBoundary = changeset_worker_e1001

### ==============================================================================
### SECTION 1: PRE-FLIGHT HEALTH CHECK (Get Metadata)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### REAL-LIFE FOOD APP ANALOGY:
### Before placing an order on Swiggy/Zomato, you open the restaurant's live menu 
### to see which dishes, toppings, and sizes are currently available to order.
### 
### In SAP terms, $metadata downloads the exact list of active entities, field types, 
### and required attributes configured in the Employee Central tenant.
### ==============================================================================
# @name getMetadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/$metadata
Authorization: Basic {{apiUser}}:{{apiPassword}}
Accept: application/xml


### ==============================================================================
### SECTION 2: DELTA CHECK / QUERY EXISTING DATA
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### REAL-LIFE FOOD APP ANALOGY:
### Checking your "Recent Orders" tab before hitting reorder, ensuring you don't 
### accidentally place a duplicate order for the same meal twice.
### 
### Here, we query active records in a department to verify connectivity and confirm 
### whether this employee already exists before creating a new profile.
### ==============================================================================
# @name queryEmpJobDelta
GET {{baseUrl}}/EmpJob?$top=5&$select=userId,startDate,department,businessUnit,customString1,customString2&$filter=customString1 eq 'OU_PUNE_TECH'
Authorization: Basic {{apiUser}}:{{apiPassword}}
Accept: application/json


### ==============================================================================
### SECTION 3: MULTIPART $BATCH INGESTION (THE SEALED DELIVERY BAG)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### REAL-LIFE FOOD APP ANALOGY:
### You order a 3-course meal: 
###   1. Starter (PerPerson)
###   2. Main Course (EmpEmployment)
###   3. Side & Dessert (EmpJob)
### 
### The restaurant places all 3 boxes inside ONE sealed delivery bag (The ChangeSet).
### 
### When the delivery rider arrives at your doorstep:
### - If all 3 items are correct, you accept the entire bag.
### - If the restaurant forgot the main course or brought the wrong dish, you REJECT 
###   the entire bag at once. You don't keep just the starter while missing the meal.
### 
### In database terms, this is ATOMICITY: all 3 tables update together, or none do.
### ==============================================================================
# @name executeBatchWorkerLoad
POST {{baseUrl}}/$batch
Authorization: Basic {{apiUser}}:{{apiPassword}}
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary={{boundary}}

--{{boundary}}
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary={{changesetBoundary}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### ITEM 1: THE STARTER / APPETIZER (PerPerson API)
### Food Analogy: Setting the foundation of the meal (Who ordered the food).
### SAP Meaning: Creates the fundamental human being record in the global database.
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--{{changesetBoundary}}
Content-Type: application/http
Content-Transfer-Encoding: binary

POST PerPerson HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
Accept: application/json

{
  "personIdExternal": "EMP_GLOBAL_1001",
  "userId": "EMP_GLOBAL_1001",
  "perPerson": {
    "customString1": "MIGRATION_SOURCE_PEOPLESOFT"
  }
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### ITEM 2: THE MAIN COURSE (EmpEmployment API)
### Food Analogy: The core meal item containing the order timestamp.
### SAP Meaning: Creates the employment contract timeline with the start date.
### Note: Date is in Epoch format (/Date(...)/) converted by our CPI Groovy script.
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--{{changesetBoundary}}
Content-Type: application/http
Content-Transfer-Encoding: binary

POST EmpEmployment HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
Accept: application/json

{
  "personIdExternal": "EMP_GLOBAL_1001",
  "userId": "EMP_GLOBAL_1001",
  "startDate": "/Date(1787562000000+0000)/",
  "isContingentWorker": false,
  "originalStartDate": "/Date(1787562000000+0000)/"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### ITEM 3: SIDES, DRINK & DESSERT (EmpJob API)
### Food Analogy: Specifying the custom toppings, drink flavor, and table seat.
### SAP Meaning: Assigns the department, business unit, location, manager, and pay grade.
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--{{changesetBoundary}}
Content-Type: application/http
Content-Transfer-Encoding: binary

POST EmpJob HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
Accept: application/json

{
  "userId": "EMP_GLOBAL_1001",
  "startDate": "/Date(1787562000000+0000)/",
  "seqNumber": "1",
  "eventReason": "HIRNEW",
  "businessUnit": "TECH_CORP",
  "department": "ENG_SUPPORT_L2",
  "location": "LOC_PUN_01",
  "customString1": "OU_PUNE_TECH",
  "customString3": "ROLE_SUPPORT_ENG",
  "customString4": "FUNC_TECH_OPS",
  "customString5": "DOM_INFRA_SUPPORT",
  "customString6": false,
  "standardHours": 40.0,
  "payGrade": "GRADE_L2_IN"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SEAL THE DELIVERY BAG (ChangeSet boundary closes here)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--{{changesetBoundary}}--

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### CLOSE THE ENTIRE HTTP BATCH PAYLOAD
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--{{boundary}}--